# bnbulls — what goes to github, and what deliberately does not.
#
# The repo is PRIVATE, but it is written as though it might one day be shown to
# someone for trust. Owner's rule: publish "only what's needed on the contract
# and front end, so people cannot full clone us but we can give trust", and
# never keys, passwords or private info.
#
# So: the VERIFIABLE artefacts are in (contracts, tests, deploy scripts, the
# frontend, the art engine). The OPERATIONAL playbook and the internal strategy
# log are out — those are the part that took the thinking, and they are not
# needed to check that the chain does what it claims.

# ── SECRETS · never, under any circumstance ─────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
!*.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.pwd
*.enc
*keystore*
*password*
# ⚠ The wallet-key vault. It lives at ~/.bnbulls-secrets, OUTSIDE this repo, so
# nothing here matches it today and NO rule above would have caught it either --
# `*keystore*` does not match the name. This exists so that a copy dropped into
# the tree by mistake can never be staged.
.bnbulls-secrets
.bnbulls-secrets/
# Machine-local editor/tooling settings. Ignored only by a global ignore on the
# box that made it, which no other clone has -- so without this line it is one
# `git add -A` away from being committed anywhere else.
.claude/

# ── build output / caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
cache/
cache_forge/
artifacts/
.buildgate/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── chain run artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `broadcast/` holds raw tx payloads from real runs, `.state/` is keeper
# cursors. Neither is source, and both leak operational detail.
broadcast/
.state/
deployments/*.json
!deployments/names.json
!deployments/rarity.json

# ── THE MOAT · the operational half of the product ──────────────────────────
# The keeper fleet is ~40 modules of bots, price keepers, alert routing, dedupe
# and containers. It is what makes the game RUN, and it is not needed by anyone
# checking that the contracts do what they say. Same for the brand render
# pipeline and the copy.
marketing/

# ── internal strategy and history ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The design log, the ops rules, the migration plan, the launch-venue research
# and the voice guide. Every one is either commercially sensitive, a record of
# mistakes, or a playbook. The contracts and their tests carry the trust story
# on their own.
DECISIONS.md
BUILD-PLAN.md
BNBULLS-BOOTSTRAP.md
KEEPER-FLEET-AND-OPS.md
LEARNINGS-AND-MISTAKES.md
DEPLOY-SAFETY-PREFLIGHT.md
VOICE-AND-BRAND.md
BNB-CHAIN-FACTS.md
FOUR-MEME-LAUNCH-ROUTE.md
POT-ASSET-SWAP-DESIGN.md
SNAPSHOT-AND-MIGRATION.md
SNAPSHOT-ANNOUNCEMENT-COPY.md

# ── the $FIGHT snapshot evidence ────────────────────────────────────────────
# 11MB of raw chain logs. Real, and worth publishing WITH the announcement so
# the numbers are checkable, but it is migration evidence rather than source.
snapshot-archive/

# ── large art review renders ────────────────────────────────────────────────
generator/art-review/
frontend/.brand-proof/

# ── third-party reference art ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The inspiration images the owner dropped in the root at kickoff. Not ours,
# not needed, and stock art of unknown licence has no business in a repo that
# might be shown to someone.
download.jpg
images*.jpg
images*.png
*.avif

# ── foundry dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vendored third-party source (OpenZeppelin, forge-std, chainlink). Restored
# with `forge install`; see the README. No reason to republish someone else's
# library, and it keeps the diff to code we actually wrote.
#
# ⚠ ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH ON PURPOSE. A bare `lib/` matches at EVERY
# depth, so it silently swallowed `contracts/lib/` too — and that is 78KB of
# PotSplitter plus TimelockedAddress, Stats and Xorshift, i.e. most of the
# money layer, missing from a repo whose entire purpose is letting someone
# verify the money layer. Caught after the first push. Do not un-anchor it.
# ── vendored foundry deps: now GIT SUBMODULES, not ignored ──────────────────
# They were ignored, and the consequence was that a fresh clone of this repo
# could not compile at all: no lib/, no .gitmodules, so forge-std, openzeppelin
# and chainlink were simply absent. Same class of mistake as the one above and
# with the same cost -- a repo whose purpose is letting someone verify the
# money layer has to BUILD for them. Git tracks a gitlink plus .gitmodules,
# not the dependency source, so nothing is bloated by this.
*.webp

# ── scratch + unpublished marketing copy ────────────────────────────────────
.scratch/
TG-ANNOUNCEMENT.md
X-ANNOUNCEMENT.md

# ── art build artefacts, written to CWD ─────────────────────────────────────
# `generator/build.mjs` calls writeFileSync("heroes.png", ...) with no path, so
# `npm run art` from the repo root drops these four here. They are regenerated
# output; the reviewed copies live in generator/. Anchored to the root so the
# tracked generator/*.png are untouched. CI runs `npm run art`, so without this
# every CI-adjacent local run leaves a dirty tree.
/heroes.png
/ladder.png
/roll.png
/weapons.png
